      "message": "Thanks for trying to make the refactoring to make the code generalized.\n\nIMHO, I feel this refactoring is making the logic a little bit hard to follow.\n\nGenerally, it will be much easier to follow the logic if we return in the early phase. So I would like to propose the following refactoring, even though it is a little bit more verbose. Basically, to avoid passing fallbackIndex down in too many level.\n\n```\nprivate int getNetworkInterfaceIndex(NsdServiceInfo serviceInfo) {\n        final Network network \u003d serviceInfo.getNetwork();\n        if (network \u003d\u003d null) {\n            return serviceInfo.getInterfaceIndex() !\u003d 0 ? serviceInfo.getInterfaceIndex() : IFACE_IDX_ANY;\n        }\n        return getNetworkInterfaceIndex(network);\n    }\n    \nprivate int getNetworkInterfaceIndex(DiscoveryRequest discoveryRequest) {\n        final Network network \u003d discoveryRequest.getNetwork();\n        if (network \u003d\u003d null) {\n            return IFACE_IDX_ANY;\n        }\n        return getNetworkInterfaceIndex(network);\n    } \n    \n    \nprivate int getNetworkInterfaceIndex(@Nullable Network network) {\n   .....\n}\n```",
